    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Dylan Beavers** headlines our lineup as our most efficient option with a 68.38 rating. His favorable matchup against Montero, K, coupled with a lead-off spot and a meaningful wind-out boost, makes him a priority start to capitalize on stolen base upside. Similarly, **Bryce Harper** (74.08) remains our anchor; despite a slight park penalty, his premium position in the three-hole against Phillips and a strong xWOBa projection make him the safest bet for production. We are also leaning heavily on **Luis Arraez** (63.97) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (63.75), both of whom benefit significantly from high-order lineup placement and SP matchups that sit comfortably above the 4.00 xERA mark.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Drew Gilbert** (51.26), who narrowly missed the cut behind the outfield rotation. While **Gilbert** offers elite speed, his matchup against the pitcher Sproat and the aggregate efficiency of **Daulton Varsho** (59.67) and **Taylor Ward** (58.97) pushed him to the reserves. We are keeping a close eye on **Yainer Diaz**; his 58.85 rating is contingent on his inclusion in the lineup, as we are currently operating under the assumption he hits 6th. **JJ Bleday** remains a marginal start (51.65) today, as his platoon disadvantage against Cecconi creates a significant performance ceiling that makes him a candidate to be benched if we see late-breaking news regarding his availability or weather shifts. \n\nAs we look across the bench, **Braden Montgomery** (44.03) and **Lawrence Butler** (43.62) remain on the outside looking in, primarily due to tougher assignments against Fried and Tolle. We are mindful that **Yainer Diaz**'s lineup status is still \"Pending,\" which introduces a minor risk factor for our C1 slot; should he be held out, we will need to pivot quickly. Overall, the priority today is maximizing the stolen base potential in the top half of the order while riding the favorable wind conditions for our outfield trio.",
